      "body": "### Godot version\n\n3.3 stable\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 20.04 | proccessor: Intel\u00ae Pentium(R) Silver N5030 CPU @ 1.10GHz \u00d7 4  | graphics: Mesa Intel\u00ae UHD Graphics 605 (GLK 3)|   HP LAPTOP BTW\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen i start it works just fine, as you can see in the screen shot. Then i try to import a project or make a new project and my computer litterly freezes on the loading screen... This is a new computer and Ive tried waiting like 30 minutes and nothing happens. Is something not supported, i know it cant be this slow right??\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT INFO?:\r\ni installed a new WiFi driver before, i don't know if that will help.\r\n\r\nI tried on earlier versions and its doesn't work\r\n64 bits Ubuntu. \r\n\r\n\r\n![Snapchat-1216963610](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/77030926/129988724-cf4520cc-8403-4d67-94e3-557be56732fb.jpg)\r\nI LATTERLY HAVE TO RESTART MY COMPUTER WHEN IT FREEZES, ive also tried with and without sudo and re downloaded it and tried nothing seem to work.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ndownload latest godot release. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project\n\nHave an identical computer, download Godot, try and run it.",
